    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1684">

                <pb facs="1430" n="1326" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.114M69/158.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 245.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my despatch No. 243, of
                    today’s date, regarding the trial of the captain of the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Texas</hi> sunk in Smyrna harbor in April last, I have
                    the honor to transmit herewith copies of two despatches<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d1684-f1"/> just received by the Embassy from the Consulate General
                    at Smyrna.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1684-a1.xml" xpointer="d1684-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1684-f1" n="4" xml:id="d1684-f1-content">
                <p>One of these is the inclosure with Mr. Horton’s No. 45 of July 9, supra.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
